@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Privacy Policy";
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<link href="@Url.Content("~/Content/cloudhub-legal.css")" rel="stylesheet" />

<header class="lg-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <nav class="lg-switch" aria-label="Legal pages">
            <a href="@Url.Action("Terms", "Legal")">Terms and Conditions</a>
            <a href="@Url.Action("Privacy", "Legal")" class="active" aria-current="page">Privacy Policy</a>
        </nav>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p>Effective date: 12 November 2026</p>
    </div>
</header>

<div class="lg-body">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="lg-grid">

            <aside class="lg-toc" aria-label="On this page">
                <h2>On this page</h2>
                <ol>
                    <li><a href="#who">Who we are</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#collect">Information we collect</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#use">How we use it</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#share">Who we share it with</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#security">How we protect it</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#retention">How long we keep it</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#cookies">Cookies</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#rights">Your rights</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#transfers">Transfers outside South Africa</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#children">Children</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#contact">Contact us</a></li>
                </ol>
            </aside>

            <article class="lg-article">

                <div class="lg-summary">
                    <strong>In short:</strong> we collect only the information we need to run your account and your hosting.
                    We store passwords as hashes, we do not sell your information, and you can ask to see, correct or delete
                    your personal information. We follow the Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA).
                </div>

                <section id="who">
                    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
                    <p>
                        <span class="lg-placeholder">[Company or team legal name]</span> operates CloudHub and is the
                        &ldquo;responsible party&rdquo; for your personal information under POPIA.
                        This policy explains what we collect, why, and what you can do about it.
                        It applies together with our <a href="@Url.Action("Terms", "Legal")">Terms and Conditions</a>.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="collect">
                    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
                    <div class="lg-table-wrap">
                        <table class="lg-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr><th>Type</th><th>What it includes</th></tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Account details</td>
                                    <td>First and last name, email address, phone number and your password (stored only as a hash, never as plain text).</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Profile choices</td>
                                    <td>Account type, organisation or institution name, what you plan to host, preferred technology and deployment method, whether you want product emails, and the date you accepted our terms.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Projects and deployments</td>
                                    <td>Project names and settings, deployment history, status and build or deployment logs.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Your content</td>
                                    <td>Source code, ZIP packages, files and database resources that you upload or connect.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Connected services</td>
                                    <td>GitHub access tokens, repository and branch details, and publishing credentials. These are stored securely and are never shown on web pages or in ordinary logs.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Billing</td>
                                    <td>Subscription history, invoices and payment records. Card payments are handled by our payment provider, and we do not intend to store full card details ourselves.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Support</td>
                                    <td>Support tickets and the replies we send.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Technical data</td>
                                    <td>Sign-in activity, error and security logs, and resource usage such as storage consumption.</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <p>You give us most of this information directly. The rest is created when you use CloudHub.</p>
                </section>

                <section id="use">
                    <h2>3. How we use it</h2>
                    <p>We use your information to:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>create and secure your account, and verify your email address;</li>
                        <li>build, deploy, host and monitor your applications;</li>
                        <li>manage your subscription, issue invoices and confirm payments;</li>
                        <li>send service emails, such as verification, password reset, deployment results and billing notices;</li>
                        <li>respond to support requests;</li>
                        <li>keep the platform secure, prevent abuse and keep audit records of important actions; and</li>
                        <li>send product updates, only if you chose to receive them.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        We process your information because it is needed to provide the service you asked for, because you have given consent,
                        because the law requires it, or because we have a legitimate interest in keeping CloudHub secure.
                        We use it only for these purposes and collect no more than we need.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="share">
                    <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
                    <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Service providers</strong> that help us run CloudHub, such as our email, payment and hosting providers, who may use it only to provide their service to us.</li>
                        <li><strong>GitHub</strong>, when you connect your account, so that we can list your repositories and fetch the code you choose to deploy.</li>
                        <li><strong>Authorities or other parties</strong>, where the law requires it or where it is needed to protect the rights and safety of CloudHub, our customers or others.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Other customers can never see your projects, logs, files or credentials.</p>
                </section>

                <section id="security">
                    <h2>5. How we protect it</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Passwords are hashed before they are saved, and email verification and password reset tokens are stored as hashes.</li>
                        <li>Customers can only access their own projects, and administrator pages are separate from customer access.</li>
                        <li>Customer builds run in isolated environments, away from the main web application.</li>
                        <li>Access tokens and publishing credentials are protected and are never displayed in ordinary logs.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        No system is completely secure. If a security breach puts your personal information at risk,
                        we will notify you and the Information Regulator as POPIA requires.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="retention">
                    <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
                    <p>
                        We keep your information while your account is active and for as long as we need it for the purposes above.
                        After you close your account we delete or anonymise it, except where we must keep it by law or for legitimate business records.
                        Invoices, subscription history and payment records are kept for the period required by South African law.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="cookies">
                    <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
                    <p>
                        CloudHub uses a sign-in cookie to keep you logged in, and security cookies that protect forms from forgery.
                        These are essential for the platform to work. If you tick &ldquo;remember me&rdquo; when you log in,
                        the sign-in cookie lasts longer. You can clear cookies in your browser at any time, but you will then be logged out.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="rights">
                    <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
                    <p>Under POPIA you may:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>ask whether we hold personal information about you, and request a copy;</li>
                        <li>ask us to correct or delete information that is inaccurate, outdated or no longer needed;</li>
                        <li>object to our processing of your information;</li>
                        <li>withdraw your consent at any time, including turning off product emails (service emails will continue while you have an account); and</li>
                        <li>complain to the Information Regulator (South Africa) if you believe your information has been mishandled.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>To use any of these rights, contact us using the details in section 12. We may need to confirm your identity first.</p>
                </section>

                <section id="transfers">
                    <h2>9. Transfers outside South Africa</h2>
                    <p>
                        Some of our service providers, such as email and payment services, may process information in other countries.
                        Where this happens, we take reasonable steps to make sure your information is protected to a similar standard.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="children">
                    <h2>10. Children</h2>
                    <p>
                        CloudHub is not intended for anyone under 18 unless a parent or legal guardian has given permission.
                        If you believe a child has registered without permission, contact us and we will take appropriate action.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="changes">
                    <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
                    <p>
                        We may update this policy. The effective date at the top shows when it last changed,
                        and we will tell you about significant changes by email or in your dashboard.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="contact">
                    <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
                    <p>
                        For privacy questions or requests, contact our Information Officer,
                        <span class="lg-placeholder">[Information Officer name]</span>, at
                        <span class="lg-placeholder">[privacy email address]</span>.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <p class="lg-footer-note">
                    Also read our <a href="@Url.Action("Terms", "Legal")">Terms and Conditions</a>.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
